# Stage 4 scheduler entry — INTENTIONALLY DISABLED. Hard rule 8 (Gate A).
#
# Nothing here runs. Every line is a comment; `crontab -l` shows no patch-watch entry.
# Uncommenting this installs live traffic, which requires all three of:
#   1. Jack's message "GATE A APPROVED" (Gate A itself; src/config.py or the env marker
#      is the mechanical switch, the message is the authorisation — see docs/OPERATIONS.md
#      for the difference between what the code checks and what the rule means);
#   2. the project page live and the User-Agent placeholders filled in
#      (assert_live_allowed() refuses on `[PROJECT_URL]` / `[CONTACT_EMAIL]`);
#   3. IRB/IT determination received (docs/IRB_INQUIRY_NOTE.md).
#
# The pilot protocol is snapshot A, then snapshot B at least six hours later, and no
# third snapshot without Jack's approval — so a daily entry is what the study BECOMES,
# not what the pilot runs. Keep it disabled through the pilot.
#
# Local time on this machine is Central Daylight Time (UTC-5); cron uses local time, and
# all timestamps in the database are stored in UTC.
#
# ── rehearsal (no network at all; safe to enable today) ────────────────────────────
# 0 4 * * 0   cd /c/Users/jforden/Desktop/repos/patch-watch && .venv/Scripts/python.exe -X utf8 scripts/run_snapshot.py --mock --label MOCK_WEEKLY >> logs/cron.out 2>&1
#
# ── live daily snapshot (DO NOT UNCOMMENT BEFORE GATE A) ────────────────────────────
# 0 9 * * *   cd /c/Users/jforden/Desktop/repos/patch-watch && .venv/Scripts/python.exe -X utf8 scripts/run_snapshot.py --label "SNAP_$(date +\%Y\%m\%d)" >> logs/cron.out 2>&1
#
# ── the pilot's second snapshot, >=6h after the first (DO NOT UNCOMMENT BEFORE GATE A) ─
# 30 15 * * * cd /c/Users/jforden/Desktop/repos/patch-watch && .venv/Scripts/python.exe -X utf8 scripts/run_snapshot.py --label "SNAP_B_$(date +\%Y\%m\%d)" >> logs/cron.out 2>&1
